DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ffiinniittee(), ffiinniitteeff(), and ffiinniitteell() functions return a nonzero value
       if _x is neither infinite nor a "not‐a‐number" (NaN) value, and 0 other‐
       wise.

       The iissnnaann(), iissnnaannff(), and iissnnaannll() functions return a nonzero value if
       _x is a NaN value, and 0 otherwise.

       The iissiinnff(), iissiinnffff(), and iissiinnffll() functions return 1 if _x is positive
       infinity, -1 if _x is negative infinity, and 0 otherwise.

